 faqTop:'05 / GOOD TO KNOW', faqHeading:'Any questions?', faqIntro:'Find more details in the', docs:'project documentation', faq:[['Is NeutronDrive an official Proton client?','No. NeutronDrive is an independent open-source project and is not supported by Proton AG. You need a Proton account with access to Proton Drive.'],['Is NeutronDrive free?','Yes. The source code is MIT licensed. There is no NeutronDrive subscription. Proton’s own plans and terms apply to Proton storage and services.'],['Which desktops are supported?','NeutronDrive is built for Linux. File-manager integration and status icons depend on the desktop and its version. GNOME needs a suitable extension for a visible tray icon. Sandboxed packages have additional limitations.'],['Are all files automatically available offline?','No. Online files are downloaded on demand. Use “Keep on device” to select files or folders for offline use. Wait for downloads to finish before disconnecting.'],['What are the beta limitations?','Among other limits, there is no multi-account interface, no Proton Docs/Sheets export and no complete advanced-link settings. Whole-folder deletion propagation remains blocked. Concurrent changes can cause conflicts; keep an independent backup.'],['How can I help?','Report reproducible bugs through GitHub Issues, review translations or contribute code. Report security vulnerabilities through the private reporting process described in SECURITY.md.']],
